{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And he called.</b> The heh of <b>lekorbah</b> is superfluous, like ולדבקה בו (Deuteronomy 11:22). A great sage erred, for he said that it is like לשמור את בריתי לעמדה (Ezekiel 17:14), for he derives the heh and the word עומד as עומדת — therefore the meaning is 'to stand in it.'"], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 36, :notes {0 "Resolved 'a great sage' without bracketing, as Ibn Ezra's referent is not specified and cannot be identified with certainty."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:40:44.054594440Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}